{"cluster_id": "C-2329", "topic": "At most one ref-log PUT per table may", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B011-099", "B012-034"], "canonical_claim": "At most one ref-log PUT per table may have an unresolved result; a later same-table PUT cannot start until the earlier result is resolved.; A ref append lane obtains `ref_sequence` from a store-wide counter, permits at most one unresolved PUT per table, blocks that table's lane while unresolved, and applies observed durable state to the cache before unwedging.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-12-cas-ref-table-snapshot-log-phase1.md#L301-L306", "docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-11-cas-ref-table-snapshot-log-design.md#writer-side-linearization"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2330", "topic": "Warm table mutations perform no ref LIST, snapshot", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B011-104"], "canonical_claim": "Warm table mutations perform no ref `LIST`, snapshot GET, `gc/state` read, HEAD, or compare-and-swap; they append one deterministic log object and update cached state.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-11-cas-ref-table-snapshot-log-design.md#common-mutation-path"]}
