{"cluster_id": "C-2333", "topic": "The ref protocol stores per-table append-only _log/<txn-id> objects", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B012-002"], "canonical_claim": "The ref protocol stores per-table append-only `_log/<txn-id>` objects and writer-published `_snap/<id>.proto` snapshots; `GC` folds per-table cursors and manifest-edge deltas from one global `LIST`, cleans covered objects, and never reconstructs table state.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-12-cas-ref-table-snapshot-log-phase1.md#L9-L12"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2334", "topic": "Ref log operations are exactly NamespaceBirth, OwnerTransition, SetPayload", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B012-022"], "canonical_claim": "Ref log operations are exactly `NamespaceBirth`, `OwnerTransition`, `SetPayload`, and `RemoveNamespace`; owner bindings distinguish `Committed` and `Precommit` owners.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-12-cas-ref-table-snapshot-log-phase1.md#L76-L85"]}
