{"cluster_id": "C-2336", "topic": "The ref batching queue creates one compatible RefLogTxn", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["B012-035"], "canonical_claim": "The ref batching queue creates one compatible `RefLogTxn`, validates requests with per-request undo against cached state, gives invalid requests their own exceptions, runs birth and removal alone, and limits each batch to one operation per ref name.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-12-cas-ref-table-snapshot-log-phase1.md#L306-L311"]}
{"cluster_id": "C-2337", "topic": "Snapshot publication is background and off-lane, uses snapshot_log_count_threshold", "target": "architecture/manifests-and-refs", "member_ids": ["AUDIT-M2-091", "B012-036"], "canonical_claim": "Snapshot publication is background and off-lane, uses `snapshot_log_count_threshold`, `snapshot_log_bytes_threshold`, mount-time triggers, and `snapshot_min_log_age_ms`, and resolves uncertain publication by exact-key byte comparison.; Ref-log snapshots publish in the background, best-effort, one in flight per table, once the tail exceeds `snapshot_log_count_threshold` (default 256 logs) or `snapshot_log_bytes_threshold` (default 1 MiB); publish failures arm per-table exponential backoff from 200 ms to 30 s.", "issue_ids": [], "sources": ["docs/superpowers/cas/11-walkthrough.md#in-s3", "docs/superpowers/plans/2026-07-12-cas-ref-table-snapshot-log-phase1.md#L322-L331"]}
